  "notes": "West leads the ♦K against 4♠. West wins the trick and continues diamonds. South's best play allows him to make the contract any time spades are 3-1 as long as hearts are no worse than 4-1. The recommended line of play will also allow South to retain trump control when East has all 4 trumps and at least 2 hearts.\n\nSouth should ruff with a middle trump at trick 2 and unblock the ♣A. A low trump is played. West shows out and East must win the ♠Q. East returns a diamond, ruffed high by South.\n\nTo prevent East from discarding hearts when dummy's clubs are played, South should cash 2 top hearts now. South next plays another low spade. East must duck as North still has a trump to handle a third diamond force.\n\nThe lead is now in dummy. Dummy's clubs are played for heart discards. If East ruffs low at any time, South can overruff and play hearts. East will get only the ♠A.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♦K against 4♠. West wins the trick and continues diamonds. South's best play allows him to make the contract any time spades are 3-1 as long as hearts are no worse than 4-1. The recommended line of play will also allow South to retain trump control when East has all 4 trumps and at least 2 hearts.",
